{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the undelivered cross-surface Work-count outcome from #4586 on the current UI. Queue after #20258 and #20424, before deployment-docs #20009; preserve current reviews, reader renewal and case-C adoption work.\n\nAt the same verified frontier #20619, the actual browser row-selection code produces open 4, while bounded gs status and HTTP status-summary print lifecycle open 1. The arithmetic is consistent: the browser grouping is open 1 + reported 1 + awaiting-review 2. The missing piece is a shared named Work summary that a reader can reconcile directly. GitHub issue #1 remains open. The [evidence and original request](count-parity-evidence.json) records the exact frontier, output, current source comparison and retirement. This is a source-function/HTTP/CLI reproduction; browser rendering was unavailable.\n\n#4586 was retired because the old Work/Activity selector was deleted, with a parenthetical promise of a separate parity check. Deleting that selector settled the sibling clutter request #4587, but did not deliver this functional counting outcome. Current [status rendering](internal/statusview/view.go@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:450) still exposes lifecycle buckets only; [browser populations](ui/src/lib/rows.ts@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:48) and [their visible counts](ui/src/components/RequestList.tsx@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:119) group them. The [status guide](docs/reference/gs/status.md@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:150) explains the arithmetic but cannot substitute for the requested behavior.\n\nDeliver one plainly labelled Work summary with the same global, unfiltered named commitment populations as the then-current browser: open, completed, closed-not-completed and lifecycle-stale while that population exists. Show the open lifecycle breakdown and commitment total. Preserve detailed lifecycle diagnostics, distinguishing lifecycle open from the grouped Work open. Preserve the overlap rules: reasoning-moved and artifact-landing-audit are subsets/audits, never extra members of the partition; awaiting-ratification counts a different duty and never enters the commitment total; artifact counts remain separate. Search/actor-scoped results must identify their scope and must not be compared as if they were global counts.\n\nGive the derived commitment classification one Go owner used by bounded and complete status rendering and the resident/MCP global summary totals. Preserve full snapshot shape compatibility deliberately; reconcile any new wire fields with browser types and shared parity checks. Independently compare the Go result with the actual browser selector on the same frozen projection, including every emitted lifecycle, ordinary stale qualifiers, all three awaiting states, multiple historical commitments for one request, landing-audit overlap, and a separate ratification duty. Do not create a second hand-maintained formula in each adapter. Keep bounded limits/omission counts and existing authority, trust and lifecycle behavior.\n\n#19939/P2 is still unadopted and this request does not authorize it. Matching current grouping is independently actionable; if P2 is adopted and lands before this implementation, update the acceptance matrix together and remove its obsolete stale population rather than reintroducing it. Do not claim that this counting task resolves P2 or that #20203 wire-field parity already delivered it.\n\nAcceptance: prove the named summary/breakdown/partition and overlapping counts at identical frontiers through actual bounded CLI, complete CLI, HTTP summary, MCP status/wait global totals and browser selector/rendered UI. Include a negative control that drops an awaiting-review member or changes one surface grouping and fails the parity check, plus search/scope controls. Update the status guide and affected architecture contracts at the same head with correct behavior provenance; run meaningful affected Go, wire parity, UI and docset gates, diff check and reproducible embed checks if UI output changes. Publish exact changed-path artifacts, independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, approved exact-head sealed landing, push and CI, and remove the owned feature branch/worktree. Report any actual browser-access block honestly; fixtures alone do not prove browser interaction. No deployment, keys, telemetry or external GitHub mutation is assigned.\n\nThis fresh assignment rests on the live, in-main behavior publications 3b062b92 (status view) and6f5ca1c3 (browser rows). Retired #4586 is historical evidence linked above, not a live authority basis. Its original retirement remains recorded.","body":{"branch":"request/shared-work-population-counts","conditions":"Deliver the original functional cross-surface named Work-count grouping on current classifications, one Go owner and actual same-frontier parity controls, preserve scope/overlap/lifecycle/authority, update docs and wire contracts, independently review/seal/push/CI/clean the exact head. No P2 adoption or live deployment.","head":"50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3b062b92c14324c245adc4cd7a3131669a37e7bb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6f5ca1c3b34c09a4a1a5f26ac366b94c748e3ca9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:012451209d3000492d2e523089e5973beec05f61, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c3db6e198fe71549257a6a3a51b408f6955d9d4, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0fae00055767520da097d824d3f7732892d47ef8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:14572ba1453f650ad7eb2714e3e2dfa974c8c8ba and 40 more","target_head":"50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f